# denylist.example - copy to denylist.local (gitignored) and fill in for real.
# bash .githooks/install.sh does the copy for you.
#
# One term or extended-regex pattern per line; lines starting with # are
# comments. The pre-commit hook and .githooks/content-audit.sh join these with |
# and grep case-insensitively over the staged additions and the tracked tree.
#
# BECAUSE THESE ARE REGEXES, ESCAPE THE PUNCTUATION IN A REAL NAME. A company
# called "Acme (Holdings" is an unbalanced parenthesis, which is not a valid
# pattern. The gate refuses rather than silently checking nothing, and it names
# the offending line, but writing "Acme \(Holdings" up front saves you the trip.
#
# SAVE THIS FILE WITH UNIX LINE ENDINGS. On Windows, a CRLF save used to disable
# the whole list invisibly: every term ended up with a trailing carriage return
# and matched nothing. The loader strips them now, but plain LF is still right.
#
# Put in everything that must never appear in this public repo: your home paths,
# personal or client domains, internal project names, and live-key shapes.
#
# NEVER COMMIT THE REAL LIST. Publishing your content scanner must never publish
# the list of things you are keeping out. That is why denylist.local is
# gitignored and this example holds only shapes.

# Home paths, all three platforms.
/Users/<your-username>
/home/<your-username>
C:\\Users\\<your-username>

# Names that mean something to you and nothing to a stranger.
my-internal-name
my-client-name
my-personal-domain\.example

# Live-key shapes.
sk-[A-Za-z0-9]{16,}
sk_live_[A-Za-z0-9]+
pk_live_[A-Za-z0-9]+
ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}
